{"id":"880c63222bbf9522e115c34418f1e8039e6ee40c","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"880c63222bbf9522e115c34418f1e8039e6ee40c","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/usage/security.md","lines":["@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ denial of service:"," | `VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_REQUEST_DOWNLOAD_SIZE_MB` | `256` | Maximum total HTTP media bytes downloaded for one request, including concurrent downloads and retried attempts. Enforced while streaming. |"," | `VLLM_MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS` | `178956970` (~179M pixels) | Maximum decoded image size in pixels. Images exceeding this are rejected before raster memory is allocated. Default matches PIL's built-in 2x decompression-bomb threshold (~680 MB for RGB). |"," | `VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_REQUEST_DECODE_BYTES` | `715827880` (~683 MiB) | Maximum aggregate decoded image, video-frame, and audio bytes in one request. Images are charged at four bytes per pixel before decoding; audio is limited before decoding; video frames are charged at three bytes per pixel after frame sampling and before decoding. |","+| `VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES` | `715827880` (~683 MiB) | Maximum estimated preprocessing bytes per prompt in the supported Python processors below. This setting is independent of the request decode budget. |"," | `VLLM_MAX_AUDIO_CLIP_FILESIZE_MB` | `25` | Maximum compressed filesize in MB for a single audio file. Enforced on all audio inputs (multimodal chat URLs, speech-to-text uploads, data: URLs, and local file paths) before decoding begins. |"," | `VLLM_MAX_AUDIO_DECODE_DURATION_S` | `600` | Maximum decoded audio duration in seconds. Prevents compressed audio from expanding into gigabytes of float32 PCM. |"," | `VLLM_MAX_AUDIO_DECODE_BYTES` | `268435456` (256 MiB) | Maximum float32 PCM bytes that audio decoding may allocate. Guards against sample-rate forgery where an inflated header sample rate bypasses the duration guard while the actual frame count causes a multi-GiB allocation. |","@@ -109,6 +110,47 @@ Setting any of these to `0` disables the corresponding limit. This is **not"," recommended** for deployments exposed to untrusted users, as it removes the"," protection against resource-exhaustion attacks."," ","+### 6. Media preprocessing limit","+","+The supported Python processors account for their allocations as follows.","+The image and video tensor checks count items processed on the current","+request. Cached items skip preprocessing, so a warm cache can admit a prompt","+that a cold cache rejects. FunAudioChat's waveform item cap runs before cache","+lookup.","+","+- FunAudioChat derives a waveform item cap from peak buffers for padding, FFT,","+  and log-Mel feature extraction. After decoding, it also counts waveform","+  copies using each clip's sample count. The configured multimodal item limit","+  applies to waveforms and `audio_embeds`.","+- Nano Nemotron VL estimates host-side image preprocessing. The CPU resize","+  path accounts for resized tiles, resize temporaries, and concatenation. It","+  includes the largest full-resolution float32 source buffer when CPU","+  normalization is enabled. The dynamic tiler charges the full-resolution","+  `uint8` images staged for upload when resizing on the device.","+- DeepSeek-VL2 and Molmo2 account for image tiles and temporary tensors before","+  materializing them.","+- DeepSeek-OCR and Unlimited-OCR account for all global views and local tiles","+  in the document plus temporary buffers for one view. Size the limit for the","+  page count and crop settings when serving long multi-page scans.","+- Qwen3-VL and LLaVA-OneVision reserve video pixel tensor bytes before each","+  clip is processed, then check the actual output bytes. Qwen3-VL also counts","+  the concatenated output while the individual tensors are live. In the Python","+  frontend, both processors accept up to 32 videos per prompt by default.","+  The Qwen3-VL default also applies to processors that","+  inherit from it: Qwen3.5, Qwen3-VL-MoE, Cosmos3, Cosmos3-Edge,","+  InternS1-Pro, InternS2-Preview, InternS2-Mobius, LFM3-VL, LFM3-Omni,","+  ColQwen3, ColQwen3.5, Alpamayo2-Super, and D3. Configure the count with","+  `--limit-mm-per-prompt.video`. Frame, size, and embedding options alone do","+  not change the default count.","+- Gemma 4 and EmbeddingGemma2 reserve video patch tensor bytes before each","+  clip is processed and account for the concatenated output while the","+  individual tensors are live. EmbeddingGemma2 counts the frames the processor","+  will keep when processor-side sampling is enabled.","+","+The Rust frontend defaults to 999 items per modality. Set an explicit video","+count of 32 in `--limit-mm-per-prompt` to match the Python default for the","+models listed above with a 32-video limit.","+"," ## Security and Firewalls: Protecting Exposed vLLM Systems"," "," While vLLM is designed to allow unsafe network services to be isolated to"],"additions":42,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/README.md","lines":["@@ -160,7 +160,11 @@ messages. Set"," placeholder ranges, for example for cache-aware routing; such a response cannot"," be sent to generate. Pass `--language-model-only` to skip multimodal"," processing, and set `--limit-mm-per-prompt` to the engine's limits so that","-render rejects the same requests.","+render enforces the same item counts. The Rust frontend defaults to 999 items","+per modality. Set an explicit video count of 32 to match the Python default","+for Qwen3-VL and its derived processors when serving those models. The","+`VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES` setting applies to supported Python","+processors."," "," Pass `--lora-modules name=path ...` to accept LoRA adapter names as the request"," `model`; rendering does not load the adapter weights, and the adapter name is"],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/render/test_launch_render.py","lines":["@@ -3,14 +3,201 @@"," \"\"\"E2E tests for render endpoints via `vllm launch` (GPU-less serving).\"\"\""," "," import httpx","+import numpy as np"," import pytest"," import pytest_asyncio"," "," from tests.utils import RemoteLaunchRenderServer","+from vllm.multimodal.utils import encode_video_url"," "," MODEL_NAME = \"vllm-project/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM\""," "," ","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"model\", \"budget\", \"cache_gb\", \"device_normalize\"),","+    [","+        (\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B\", 512 * 1024, 0, True),","+        (\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B\", 2 * 1024**2, 0, False),","+        (\"llava-hf/llava-onevision-qwen2-0.5b-ov-hf\", 3 * 1024**2, 1, True),","+        (\"google/gemma-4-E2B-it\", 6 * 1024**2, 0, True),","+    ],","+)","+def test_chat_render_rejects_over_budget_video_tensors(","+    model: str, budget: int, cache_gb: int, device_normalize: bool","+):","+    \"\"\"Each clip fits alone, but the combined preprocessing tensors do not.\"\"\"","+    args = [","+        \"--host\",","+        \"127.0.0.1\",","+        \"--dtype\",","+        \"float32\",","+        \"--max-model-len\",","+        \"4096\",","+        \"--limit-mm-per-prompt\",","+        '{\"image\": 0, \"video\": 2}',","+        \"--mm-processor-cache-gb\",","+        str(cache_gb),","+        (","+            \"--mm-device-do-normalize\"","+            if device_normalize","+            else \"--no-mm-device-do-normalize\"","+        ),","+    ]","+    videos = [","+        {\"type\": \"video_url\", \"video_url\": {\"url\": encode_video_url(frames)}}","+        for frames in (","+            np.zeros((4, 128, 128, 3), dtype=np.uint8),","+            np.full((4, 128, 128, 3), 128, dtype=np.uint8),","+        )","+    ]","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(","+        model,","+        args,","+        env_dict={\"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\": str(budget)},","+    ) as server:","+        url = server.url_for(\"v1/chat/completions/render\")","+        response = httpx.post(","+            url,","+            json={\"model\": model, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": videos}]},","+            timeout=30,","+        )","+        assert response.status_code == 400, response.text[:1000]","+        assert (","+            \"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\" in response.json()[\"error\"][\"message\"]","+        )","+","+        for video in videos:","+            response = httpx.post(","+                url,","+                json={","+                    \"model\": model,","+                    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [video]}],","+                },","+                timeout=30,","+            )","+            assert response.status_code == 200, response.text[:1000]","+","+        if cache_gb:","+            response = httpx.post(","+                url,","+                json={","+                    \"model\": model,","+                    \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": videos}],","+                },","+                timeout=30,","+            )","+            assert response.status_code == 200, response.text[:1000]","+","+","+def test_chat_render_llava_video_budget_uses_effective_options():","+    model = \"llava-hf/llava-onevision-qwen2-0.5b-ov-hf\"","+    # Two float32 frames fit without resizing, but exceed the budget at 384x384.","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(","+        model,","+        [","+            \"--host\",","+            \"127.0.0.1\",","+            \"--dtype\",","+            \"float32\",","+            \"--mm-processor-cache-gb\",","+            \"0\",","+            \"--no-mm-device-do-normalize\",","+            \"--trust-request-mm-kwargs\",","+        ],","+        env_dict={\"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\": str(64 * 1024)},","+    ) as server:","+        url = server.url_for(\"v1/chat/completions/render\")","+        for frame_count, videos_kwargs, status in (","+            (2, {\"do_resize\": False}, 200),","+            (2, {\"size\": {\"shortest_edge\": 24}}, 200),","+            (2, {}, 400),","+            (2, {\"size\": {\"height\": \"invalid\", \"width\": 24}}, 400),","+            (6, {\"do_resize\": False, \"do_sample_frames\": True, \"num_frames\": 2}, 200),","+        ):","+            video_url = encode_video_url(","+                np.zeros((frame_count, 32, 48, 3), dtype=np.uint8)","+            )","+            response = httpx.post(","+                url,","+                json={","+                    \"model\": model,","+                    \"messages\": [","+                        {","+                            \"role\": \"user\",","+                            \"content\": [","+                                {\"type\": \"video_url\", \"video_url\": {\"url\": video_url}}","+                            ],","+                        }","+                    ],","+                    \"mm_processor_kwargs\": {\"videos_kwargs\": videos_kwargs},","+                },","+                timeout=30,","+            )","+            assert response.status_code == status, response.text[:1000]","+            if not videos_kwargs:","+                error = response.json()[\"error\"][\"message\"]","+                assert \"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\" in error","+","+","+def test_chat_render_gemma4_video_budget_uses_image_processor_options():","+    model = \"google/gemma-4-E2B-it\"","+    video_url = encode_video_url(np.zeros((2, 96, 96, 3), dtype=np.uint8))","+    # With device normalization both frames are uint8. Float32 frames would","+    # exceed the same budget because the output is concatenated.","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(","+        model,","+        [","+            \"--host\",","+            \"127.0.0.1\",","+            \"--dtype\",","+            \"float32\",","+            \"--max-model-len\",","+            \"4096\",","+            \"--mm-processor-cache-gb\",","+            \"0\",","+            \"--mm-device-do-normalize\",","+            \"--trust-request-mm-kwargs\",","+        ],","+        env_dict={\"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\": str(2 * 1024**2)},","+    ) as server:","+        response = httpx.post(","+            server.url_for(\"v1/chat/completions/render\"),","+            json={","+                \"model\": model,","+                \"messages\": [","+                    {","+                        \"role\": \"user\",","+                        \"content\": [","+                            {\"type\": \"video_url\", \"video_url\": {\"url\": video_url}}","+                        ],","+                    }","+                ],","+                \"mm_processor_kwargs\": {\"videos_kwargs\": {\"do_normalize\": True}},","+            },","+            timeout=30,","+        )","+","+    assert response.status_code == 200, response.text[:1000]","+","+","+def test_chat_render_video_options_keep_default_count_limit():","+    model = \"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B\"","+    video_url = encode_video_url(np.zeros((4, 16, 16, 3), dtype=np.uint8))","+    content = [{\"type\": \"video_url\", \"video_url\": {\"url\": video_url}}] * 33","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(","+        model,","+        [\"--limit-mm-per-prompt\", '{\"video\": {\"num_frames\": 4}}'],","+    ) as server:","+        response = httpx.post(","+            server.url_for(\"v1/chat/completions/render\"),","+            json={\"model\": model, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": content}]},","+            timeout=30,","+        )","+","+    assert response.status_code == 400, response.text[:1000]","+    assert \"At most 32 video\" in response.json()[\"error\"][\"message\"]","+","+"," @pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")"," def server():","     args: list[str] = []"],"additions":187,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_deepseek_vl2.py","lines":["@@ -1,18 +1,197 @@"," # SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0"," # SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project"," ","+import json","+","+import httpx","+import numpy as np"," import pytest"," import torch"," from PIL import Image","+from tokenizers import Tokenizer","+from tokenizers.models import WordLevel","+from transformers import TokenizersBackend"," ","+from tests.utils import RemoteLaunchRenderServer","+from vllm import envs"," from vllm.config import ModelConfig","+from vllm.exceptions import VLLMValidationError"," from vllm.multimodal import MULTIMODAL_REGISTRY","-from vllm.multimodal.processing.context import TimingContext","+from vllm.multimodal.processing.context import TimingContext, profiling_media"," from vllm.multimodal.processing.inputs import ProcessorInputs","+from vllm.multimodal.utils import encode_image_url","+from vllm.transformers_utils.configs.deepseek_vl2 import DeepseekVLV2Config","+from vllm.transformers_utils.processors.deepseek_ocr import DeepseekOCRProcessor","+from vllm.transformers_utils.processors.deepseek_vl2 import DeepseekVLV2Processor","+from vllm.transformers_utils.processors.unlimited_ocr import (","+    UnlimitedOCR2Processor,","+    UnlimitedOCRProcessor,","+)"," "," from ...utils import build_model_context"," "," ","+def _make_tokenizer():","+    tokens = (\"[UNK]\", \"<s>\", \"</s>\", \"<image>\")","+    vocab = {token: index for index, token in enumerate(tokens)}","+    return TokenizersBackend(","+        tokenizer_object=Tokenizer(WordLevel(vocab, unk_token=\"[UNK]\")),","+        unk_token=\"[UNK]\",","+        bos_token=\"<s>\",","+        eos_token=\"</s>\",","+        additional_special_tokens=[\"<image>\"],","+        chat_template=\"{% for message in messages %}{{ message.content }}{% endfor %}\",","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.skip_global_cleanup","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"architecture\", \"image_size\", \"count\", \"view_count\"),","+    [","+        (\"vl2\", (8, 8), 3, 6),","+        (\"vl2\", (32, 16), 1, 3),","+        (\"ocr\", (8, 8), 2, 2),","+        (\"ocr2\", (32, 16), 1, 3),","+    ],","+)","+def test_image_preprocessing_budget(","+    monkeypatch, architecture, image_size, count, view_count","+):","+    tokenizer = _make_tokenizer()","+    prompt = \"<image>\" * count","+    images = [Image.new(\"RGB\", image_size)] * count","+    if architecture == \"vl2\":","+        processor = DeepseekVLV2Processor(","+            tokenizer=tokenizer,","+            candidate_resolutions=((16, 16), (32, 16)),","+            patch_size=4,","+            downsample_ratio=2,","+        )","+        inputs = {\"text\": prompt, \"images\": [np.array(image) for image in images]}","+    else:","+        processor = DeepseekOCRProcessor(","+            tokenizer=tokenizer,","+            base_size=16,","+            image_size=16,","+            max_crops=2,","+            strategy=\"v1\" if architecture == \"ocr\" else \"v2\",","+        )","+        inputs = {\"prompt\": prompt, \"images\": images}","+","+    view_bytes = 3 * 16 * 16 * 4","+    required_bytes = 2 * view_count if architecture == \"vl2\" else view_count + 2","+    required_bytes *= view_bytes","+    limit = \"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\"","+    monkeypatch.setattr(envs, limit, required_bytes - 1)","+    with pytest.raises(VLLMValidationError, match=\"Image preprocessing exceeds\"):","+        processor(**inputs)","+    with profiling_media():","+        processor(**inputs)","+    with pytest.raises(VLLMValidationError, match=\"Image preprocessing exceeds\"):","+        processor(**inputs)","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(envs, limit, required_bytes)","+    at_limit = processor(**inputs)","+    monkeypatch.setattr(envs, limit, 0)","+    unlimited = processor(**inputs)","+    assert len(at_limit[\"pixel_values\"]) + len(at_limit.get(\"images_crop\", ())) == (","+        view_count","+    )","+    torch.testing.assert_close(at_limit.data, unlimited.data, rtol=0, atol=0)","+","+","+@pytest.mark.skip_global_cleanup","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"processor_cls\", \"kwargs\", \"page_size\", \"page_count\", \"tiles_per_page\"),","+    [","+        (DeepseekOCRProcessor, {}, (2480, 3508), 9, 6),","+        (UnlimitedOCRProcessor, {}, (2550, 3300), 29, 0),","+        (","+            UnlimitedOCR2Processor,","+            {\"strategy\": \"v2\", \"max_crops\": 16},","+            (2550, 3300),","+            6,","+            12,","+        ),","+    ],","+)","+def test_default_ocr_budget_accepts_multipage_scans(","+    monkeypatch, processor_cls, kwargs, page_size, page_count, tiles_per_page","+):","+    monkeypatch.delenv(\"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\", raising=False)","+    processor = processor_cls(tokenizer=_make_tokenizer(), **kwargs)","+    page = Image.new(\"RGB\", page_size, \"white\")","+    result = processor(prompt=\"<image>\" * page_count, images=[page] * page_count)","+    assert result[\"pixel_values\"].shape == (page_count, 3, 1024, 1024)","+    assert result[\"images_crop\"].shape == (page_count * tiles_per_page, 3, 640, 640)","+    assert (result[\"pixel_values\"][:, :, 512, 512] == 1).all()","+","+","+@pytest.mark.skip_global_cleanup","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"ocr\", [False, True], ids=[\"vl2\", \"ocr\"])","+def test_http_rejects_image_preprocessing_over_budget(tmp_path, ocr):","+    config = DeepseekVLV2Config(","+        architectures=[\"DeepseekOCRForCausalLM\" if ocr else \"DeepseekVLV2ForCausalLM\"],","+        tile_tag=\"2D\",","+        candidate_resolutions=((16, 16),),","+    ).to_dict()","+    config[\"language_config\"] = config.pop(\"text_config\")","+    (tmp_path / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(config))","+    if ocr:","+        DeepseekOCRProcessor(tokenizer=_make_tokenizer()).save_pretrained(tmp_path)","+        # Three global views and one view's scratch fit; four global views do not.","+        limit, accepted_count, max_model_len = 64 * (1 << 20), 3, \"2048\"","+    else:","+        DeepseekVLV2Processor(","+            tokenizer=_make_tokenizer(),","+            candidate_resolutions=((16, 16),),","+            patch_size=4,","+            downsample_ratio=2,","+        ).save_pretrained(tmp_path)","+        limit, accepted_count, max_model_len = 27000, 1, \"128\"","+","+    content = [","+        {","+            \"type\": \"image_url\",","+            \"image_url\": {\"url\": encode_image_url(Image.new(\"RGB\", (8, 8), color))},","+        }","+        for color in (\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\", \"white\")[: 4 if ocr else 3]","+    ]","+    model = str(tmp_path)","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(","+        model,","+        [","+            \"--host\",","+            \"127.0.0.1\",","+            \"--dtype\",","+            \"float32\",","+            \"--max-model-len\",","+            max_model_len,","+            \"--mm-processor-cache-gb\",","+            \"0\",","+        ],","+        env_dict={\"VLLM_MAX_MEDIA_PREPROCESSING_BYTES\": str(limit)},","+    ) as server:","+        for route in (\"v1/chat/completions/render\", \"tokenize\"):","+            for images, expected_status in (","+                (content, 400),","+                (content[:accepted_count], 200),","+            ):","+                response = httpx.post(","+                    server.url_for(route),","+                    json={","+                        \"model\": model,","+                        \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": images}],","+                    },","+                )","+                assert response.status_code == expected_status, response.text[:512]","+                if expected_status == 400:","+                    assert (","+                        \"Image preprocessing exceeds\"","+                        in response.json()[\"error\"][\"message\"]","+                    )","+","+"," @pytest.fixture"," def processor():","     config = ModelConfig(","@@ -24,6 +203,27 @@ def processor():","     return MULTIMODAL_REGISTRY.create_processor(config)"," "," ","+def test_profiling_dummy_image_ignores_request_budget(tmp_path, monkeypatch):","+    config = DeepseekVLV2Config(","+        architectures=[\"DeepseekVLV2ForCausalLM\"],","+   